not 230, and the scope was tagpu/ddraw and never "the repo" -- tagpu/src/tagpu.c:55 carries a
LIVE wglGetProcAddress call, in the other DLL, so the safety conclusion stands but "nowhere else"
did not. 22 exports, not 44 (44 is the Export Address Table and the Name-Pointer table counted
together: the same 22 symbols twice). gl-sites reads 0/0 across ITS file set, tagpu/ddraw/src,
which its own docstring says excludes tagpu/src/** and tools/ -- both still carry GL (5/6 and
8/19), so "no file in the tree" was false. 169 render_ogl lines at HEAD, not 168, and the
breakdown mixed main's counts with HEAD's. 82 PFN pointers resolved through 59
xwglGetProcAddress calls, not "98 trampolines" (98 is gl-sites' wide call count). 7 619 lines of
files, 7 623 including render_gdi.c's four -- two notes gave different numbers for the same
thing. The histogram's region was undocumented and was the anomaly's own bounding box; under
11-5f's world rect the same frame gives 83.8 %, and its bins were half-open without saying so.
"exactly that coloured set" is 74 % of it. And `1b.` is not an ordered-list marker, so two items
rendered as literal text in the wiki.

MEASURED. one-unit, four arms interleaved mainA brA mainB brB, both arms clean-built, gui.on=1.
cross-build 45 / 49 / 45 / 1 px; controls 48 and 44. The derived box is 1x1 at (512,384), the
fixture's own oscillating cursor, which the control puts a pixel in too. OUTSIDE THE MINIMAP AND
THAT PIXEL: 0 px on all four cross-build pairings. Census 749 452 on every arm. Zero VK_ERROR /
validation lines, one `gui: layer ON` each, ZERO oglu/opengl/wgl log lines on either build and no
GDI fall-back on any arm -- so nothing regressed into software rendering when the loader went.

ATTEMPT 1 FAILED GATE 1, and that is the comparator working. brB's three grabs disagreed pairwise
by 54 657 / 11 202 / 43 455 px and cmp_x.py refused to report any number, exiting "GATE 1 FAILED
... the fixture is drifting, not settling." That is the same-day fix -- choose the settled grab by
AGREEMENT rather than by index -- catching a real failure on its first outing. Attempt 2, where
all four arms settled, is the table above. (The review then showed the cause is tearing in the
fourth arm, not drift, which makes the refusal right for a reason nobody had yet.)

THE REVIEW FIXES DID NOT MOVE THE BINARY: .text, .rdata and .data are byte-identical to the DLL
the A/B measured, and zero .c/.h files changed after it, so the measurement carries. (D3's did
move, by 176 bytes, and was re-run rather than inherited.)

